The Apex Court holds that in the event the accused in the PMLA or whose allegations are linked to any persons in the predicate offence such accused in the predicate offence gets a clean chit on three circumstances - one by acquittal after a full blow trial;
two on discharge by the competent Court and three on the proceedings being quashed by the High Court in exercise of its jurisdiction under Section 482 of the Cr.P.C.
